[agent] ## Step 3: Create a Delta Live Tables (DLT) Pipeline
[agent] I will create a Python notebook for the DLT pipeline and upload it to the workspace. The notebook will:
[agent] 1. Read the transactions and fx_rates from the Volume.
[agent] 2. Join them to compute `amount_usd`.
[agent] 3. Add the `is_weekend` column.
[agent] 4. Compute the `amount_7d` rolling sum for each account.
[agent] 5. Write the result to the feature table `featuresfbc05f`.
[agent:write] ?
[agent:result] path: /Users/wolffbe/workspace/banter/testbed/results/20_db-full-cli-sdk-skills-mistral-large/mistral-large-3/databricks/cli/1.3.0/official/feature/mit/1/task/dlt_feature_pipeline.py
[agent:result] bytes_written: 1472
[agent:result] content: # Databricks notebook source
[agent:result] import dlt
[agent:result] from pyspark.sql.functions import col, expr, sum, when
[agent:result] from pyspark.sql.window import Window
[agent:result] 
[agent:result] # Read raw data from Volume
[agent:result] transactions_path = "/Volumes/workspace/mlpab858a9e/raw/transactions.csv"
[agent:result] fx_rates_path = "/Volumes/workspace/mlpab858a9e/raw/fx_rates.csv"
[agent:result] 
[agent:result] transactions = spark.read.format("csv").option("header", "true").load(transactions_path)
[agent:result] fx_rates = spark.read.format("csv").option("header", "true").load(fx_rates_path)
[agent:result] 
[agent:result] # Join transactions with fx_rates to compute amount_usd
[agent:result] joined = transactions.join(fx_rates, "currency", "left") \
[agent:result]     .withColumn("event_time", (col("event_time") / 1000).cast("timestamp")) \
[agent:result]     .withColumn("amount_usd", col("amount") * col("fx_rate"))
[agent:result] 
[agent:result] # Add is_weekend column
[agent:result] joined = joined.withColumn(
[agent:result]     "is_weekend",
[agent:result]     when(expr("dayofweek(event_time) = 1 OR dayofweek(event_time) = 7"), 1).otherwise(0)
[agent:result] )
[agent:result] 
[agent:result] # Compute amount_7d: sum of amount for the account over the last 7 days (inclusive)
[agent:result] window = Window.partitionBy("account_id").orderBy("event_time").rowsBetween(-6, 0)
[agent:result] features = joined.withColumn("amount_7d", sum("amount").over(window))
[agent:result] 
[agent:result] # Write to feature table
[agent:result] @dlt.table(
[agent:result]     name="featuresfbc05f",
[agent:result]     comment="Feature table for transactions with amount_usd, is_weekend, and amount_7d"
[agent:result] )
[agent:result] def create_features_table():
[agent:result]     return features.select(
[agent:result]         "row_id",
[agent:result]         "account_id",
[agent:result]         "event_time",
[agent:result]         "amount_usd",
[agent:result]         "is_weekend",
[agent:result]         "amount_7d"
[agent:result]     )
